 ## Background
-The method was introduced in the context of 4D mesh reconstruction from time-varying voxelized geometry [S1, unofficial]. It builds on the As-Rigid-As-Possible (ARAP) deformation method [SA07] by introducing a sparse set of anchors guided by curvature and motion correspondence scores [PGK02, BLNL14]. The method was developed to handle the noise inherent in voxel-based motion tracking, providing a robust global deformation step before local regularization [S1, unofficial].
